  {
    id: 'm17',
    title: 'Apples on the Road',
    type: '记叙',
    exam: '中考',
    words: 107,
    prompt: '下面四幅图画讲述了你上周五放学路上的一段经历：①一位老爷爷的纸袋破了，苹果滚了一地；②你和同学跑过去帮忙捡苹果；③你把自己的袋子借给他装苹果；④老爷爷笑着道谢，你们挥手告别。请根据图画内容写一篇短文，叙述这件事并写出你的感受。',
    essay: [
      'Last Friday afternoon, I was walking home from school when I saw an old man standing by the road, looking worried. His paper bag had broken, and his apples were rolling everywhere.',
      'My classmate Lin Tao and I ran up at once. "Don\'t worry, Grandpa, we will help you," I said. We picked up every apple while he thanked us again and again. Then I put the apples into my own bag and handed it back to him.',
      'The old man smiled and waved goodbye. On my way home, Lin Tao and I felt proud, because such a small act of kindness made both of us happy.',
    ],
    zh: [
      '上周五下午，我放学走路回家时，看见一位老爷爷站在路边，一脸着急。他的纸袋破了，苹果滚得到处都是。',
      '我和同学林涛立刻跑了上去。“别担心，爷爷，我们来帮您。”我说。我们把苹果一个一个捡了起来，他不停地道谢。然后我把苹果装进自己的袋子，还给了他。',
      '老爷爷笑着挥手道别。回家路上，我和林涛都很自豪，因为这样一个小小的善举，我们两个人都特别开心。',
    ],
    expressions: ['was walking home from school when...', 'at once', 'again and again', 'handed it back to him', 'a small act of kindness'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm18',
    title: 'Congratulations, Chris!',
    type: '书信',
    exam: '高考',
    words: 249,
    prompt: '假定你是李华，你的英国朋友 Chris 作为交换生在你校学习，上周五他在学校“用英语讲中国故事”演讲比赛中获得一等奖。请给他写一封邮件，祝贺他的成绩，回顾他备赛的努力，并邀他参加班里为他准备的小型庆祝会。',
    essay: [
      'Dear Chris,',
      'I am writing with a big smile on my face: congratulations on winning first prize in our school\'s "Telling China\'s Stories in English" contest! When the host read out your name on Friday, the whole hall broke into cheers, and our class jumped up as if we had won together.',
      'Nobody who heard your speech was surprised. You took us straight into the kitchen of your host family, where Mrs. Zhao taught you to wrap zongzi before the Dragon Boat Festival. The sticky rice, the green reed leaves and Mrs. Zhao\'s laughter came alive under your words, and for three minutes you never once looked down at your notes.',
      'What impresses me most, however, is the month behind the prize. I saw you staying in the classroom after dinner, marking every pause on your script and reading it softly to the wall. When "zongzi" kept tripping you up, you asked Mrs. Zhao again and again until it sounded natural. You once told me that a good speech is rehearsed a hundred times, and you proved it yourself.',
      'Our class is planning a small celebration for you this Friday afternoon, right after the last class, and everyone hopes you will come and tell us the story behind your story. Please do not refuse — the cake is already ordered in your name.',
      'Once again, congratulations. May this prize be the first of many, and may your English keep opening new doors for you.',
      'Yours sincerely,',
      'Li Hua',
    ],
    zh: [
      '亲爱的 Chris：',
      '我写这封信时脸上一直挂着大大的笑容：祝贺你在我们学校“用英语讲中国故事”比赛中获得一等奖！周五主持人念出你名字的那一刻，整个礼堂欢呼起来，我们班同学跳了起来，好像我们一起赢了。',
      '听过你演讲的人都不意外。你把我们直接带进了寄宿家庭的厨房——端午节前，赵阿姨就在那里教你包粽子。黏黏的糯米、青青的箬叶、赵阿姨的笑声，都在你的讲述里活了起来，整整三分钟，你一次都没低头看讲稿。',
      '不过最打动我的，是奖杯背后那一个月。我看见你晚饭后留在教室，在讲稿上标出每一处停顿，对着墙壁轻声朗读。“zongzi”这个词总跟你捣乱，你就一遍又一遍地请教赵阿姨，直到它听起来自然。你说过，一场好演讲要排练一百遍，你用行动证明了自己。',
      '我们班打算本周五最后一节课后为你办一个小型庆祝会，大家都盼你能来，讲讲这个故事背后的故事。请别推辞——蛋糕已经用你的名字订好了。',
      '再次祝贺你。愿这只是你众多奖项里的第一个，愿你的英语为你打开更多扇门。',
      '此致',
      '李华',
    ],
    expressions: ['Congratulations on winning first prize in...', 'broke into cheers', 'came alive under your words', 'the month behind the prize', 'a good speech is rehearsed a hundred times', 'the story behind your story', 'May this prize be the first of many'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm19',
    title: 'Asking About the Summer English Camp',
    type: '书信',
    exam: '通用',
    words: 149,
    prompt: '假定你是李华，你在学校公告栏看到一场暑期英语研学营的招募通知。请给组织方写一封咨询邮件，询问开营时间、住宿安排与费用细节，语气礼貌。',
    essay: [
      'Dear Sir or Madam,',
      'I am Li Hua from Sunshine Middle School. I saw your notice about the summer English camp on our school notice board, and the two weeks in London sound wonderful. I would like to join, but before I fill in the form, I have a few questions.',
      'First, could you tell me the exact dates? My family will travel in early August, so I need to know whether the camp starts before July 20. Second, where will we stay, and will two students share one room?',
      'Last, how much does the camp cost, and does the price include meals, lessons and the airport transfer? Also, will there be a short level test before the first class?',
      'I would appreciate it if you could reply at your earliest convenience, so that I can send my form in time. Thank you very much.',
      'Yours faithfully,',
      'Li Hua',
    ],
    zh: [
      '尊敬的负责人：',
      '我是阳光中学学生李华。我在学校公告栏看到了你们暑期英语研学营的通知，在伦敦的两周听起来太棒了。我很想报名，但在填表之前，有几个问题想先问清楚。',
      '第一，能否告诉我确切的日期？我家人八月初要出行，所以我需要知道研学营是否在 7 月 20 日之前开营。第二，我们住在哪里？两名学生会合住一个房间吗？',
      '最后，研学营费用是多少？价格里含不含餐费、课程和机场接送？另外，第一次上课前有简短的分级测试吗？',
      '如能尽早回复，让我来得及寄出报名表，我将不胜感激。非常感谢。',
      '此致',
      '李华',
    ],
    expressions: ['I saw your notice about...', 'sound wonderful', 'before I fill in the form', 'whether the camp starts before...', 'at your earliest convenience', 'so that I can... in time'],
  },
